From 34eb46055bf3c3d3c3c119b0edc19571b8b67eda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:16:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app): a probe-only program's stock sim judges the
 uncut stock

A touch probe stays out of the program sim's plan (it removes nothing),
so a probe-only program sized the stock lattice by min(radius) over no
tools = +inf, and the grid refused the infinite cell as "invalid stock
simulation setup: ... box non-empty ..." - the wrong cause, shown on
every probe-only post. stock_grid now sizes the lattice by the stock's
span when no tool radius is finite; the sim judges the uncut stock
(clean when it is the part). A missing or invalid stock still refuses
by its own name.

Pinned by probe_only_sim::a_probe_only_program_is_judged_not_refused_as_an_invalid_setup
(fails without the fix) and ::a_probe_only_program_without_a_stock_still_says_why.

Fixes #592

